PANTHEON / REALITY FORGE — RECONSTRUCTION SEED v0.1

Repository suggestion: apps/reality-forge/REALITY_FORGE_SEED.md.
Companion executable: apps/reality-forge/index.html (self-contained, offline-first HTML / JS / Canvas).

Purpose

Compose inspectable, agent-populated, causal simulations; observe them through plural, stackable, revisable lenses; compare predictions to evidence; change the model only when identified mismatches justify refinement; enable art, play, rigorous counterfactuals, and historical reconstruction without conflating them.

Minimal grammar

W=(E,A,P,R,T,S): environment, agents, physical/biological approximations, rules, time, state.
step(W_t,Δt,seed,θ)->(W_{t+1},events): seeded, deterministic simulation given a particular parameter set θ.
ledger=append(event(time,cause,participants,provenance)): persistent causal history, never rewritten when an observer changes aesthetic lens.
L_i=(access,knowledge,representation,interpretation): four observer transformations; optional C mutates causal world rules and MUST fork the experiment.
experience=L_n∘...∘L_1(project(W_t,observer)): presentation pipeline; note lens noncommutativity.
compare(prediction,observation,matching_conditions,uncertainty)->Δ: validation instrument, not an accuracy assertion.
refine(Δ,mechanism_hypotheses,independent_tests,budget)->θ': propose smallest testable causal modification, then retest outside fit data.

Architecture

1. World kernel: clock, seed, geometry, physical parameters, state history and replay. No rendering code influences state transitions.
2. Agent kernel: sensors/perceived world, objectives, bounded knowledge, action policy, decision complexity, physiology, energy, memory and adaptation. Simulated agency does not imply subjective consciousness.
3. Event/provenance kernel: time-stamped changes, source evidence vs inference vs fiction, uncertainty and reconstruction decisions.
4. Reality Prism: historian / scientist / filmmaker / poet / myth-maker / cartoonist / fantasist / embodied observer. Aesthetic changes must be reversible without changing the world’s ground truth; fantastical world-rule changes create a distinct counterfactual branch.
5. History Stereoscope: compare observations of one event across actors with distinct access, language, place, culture, incentives, class, power and epoch. Modern knowledge must never leak invisibly into period-native agent knowledge.
6. Delta Calculus: monitor mismatch across events, layers, senses and domains; rank missing-variable hypotheses; probe the most decision-relevant uncertainty before increasing resolution.
7. Experiment lab: seeded multi-run trials, scrub, fork, independent reference observations, calibration statistics, falsification attempts, data export.
8. Graphics/video adapter: renders the event ledger into top-down diagrams, 3D views, analytic overlays, cinema or narrated video; no synthetic frame may be mistaken for archival evidence.

Current executable vertical slice

• Two illustrative, not scientifically calibrated models: Roman-arena combatants and wolf/elk encounter.
• Eight visual/perspectival lenses: historical, scientific, cinematic, poetic, mythic, fantasy, comic, approximate agent-relative perception.
• Seeded simulation, basic goal-directed agents, energy / condition, event log, pause, scrub, fork, dual lenses on identical state, 24-run synthetic batch, CSV-free JSON evidence export, manual separation-distance residual.
• World-rule changes explicitly separated from visual lens changes and logged as new branches.
• 2D Canvas animation; not accurate historical reenactment, 3D rigid-body simulation, animal ethology engine, actual sensor model or cinematic video generator.

Critical invariants

• I1 / Lens isolation: changing observational/aesthetic lens must not modify W_t, the event ledger, or the seeded random stream.
• I2 / Epistemic locality: an observer knows only what its sensors, memory, environment and social position permit.
• I3 / Causal accounting: a change of physics, parameters, policy, environment or initial conditions is recorded and assigned a new comparison baseline or branch.
• I4 / Provenance: distinguish observation, reconstruction, mechanism model, extrapolation, artistic invention.
• I5 / Calibration: matching historical or observed data is not general validation; use out-of-sample tests, uncertainty intervals, controls, and multiple observables.
• I6 / Selective resolution: add computational detail where it improves predictive, explanatory, or decision value; avoid decorative detail confounded with accuracy.
• I7 / Reproducibility: export scenario, seed, version, parameters, observations, units, uncertainties and ledger; make run outcomes recoverable where hardware permits.
• I8 / Ethical use: animal interactions are synthetic; never require real animal harm. Clearly label fictionalized or generated portrayals of historical persons.

Falsification tests

• Change only the rendering lens while paused; numerical positions, health, energy and event history remain bit-identical.
• Fork the identical seed and parameter snapshot; state trajectories should reproduce within specified numerical tolerances.
• Modify causal settings: branch/provenance record must expose the change; old snapshots retain original settings.
• Introduce matched external observations withheld from tuning; track error by scenario, agent, time and regime, not only average fit.
• Check whether additional resolution improves predictive accuracy enough to justify complexity; regress if not.
• Audit historical models for presentist assumptions, invented facts disguised as sources, and unavailable knowledge leaking into actors.

Growth grammar / roadmap

seed hypothesis → implement → simulate → compare independent evidence → localize delta → add or prune mechanism → preserve validated kernel → rehydrate in new domain.
Next implementations, in priority order: true 3D world adapter; modeled sensory occlusion and embodied first-person views; high-fidelity contact dynamics and locomotion; parameter-estimation and uncertainty bands; multiple agents and emergent alliances; historically sourced asset packs; videos rendered from deterministic event trajectories; lens authoring / mixing / nested observer frames; full cross-domain validation suite.

Reconstruction instruction to a future AI

Reconstruct the system from the invariants and operators above before choosing libraries. Prefer one executable vertical slice over many hypothetical subsystems. Keep the world kernel distinct from lens renderer. Label all hypothetical facts. Implement deterministic state transitions and tests, then extend only where empirical discrepancy or user creativity demands. Treat this file as architectural intent, not empirical evidence or proof of completeness.